Chapter: ImapWire
  cites Net chapter ImapClient

 `ImapClient` had never compiled, and the reason it had
 never compiled is the reason it needed this test: nothing cites it that
 anything else cites, so no battery run ever asked it to build. A chapter
 nobody compiles accumulates defects at leisure, and this one had two
 beyond the twelve that stopped the lexer.

 The bytes are the test, not the command text. `imap-cmd-*` answers a
 command and no terminator, because CCE has no carriage return to put in
 a literal; `imap-line-bytes` adds CRLF as the bytes 13 and 10 at the
 wire boundary. Asserting the Text would pin the half that was never
 wrong.

 And the alphabet is the other half. `imap-text-to-bytes` used
 `char-code-at` alone, which answers the CCE code point: `A` is 41 in CCE
 and 65 on the wire. Every command this chapter framed, and every XOAUTH2
 credential it base64-encoded, was in the wrong alphabet. A round-trip
 through our own encoder cannot see that -- both halves agree on CCE --
 so the expected bytes below are written out as the ASCII a reader can
 check against the RFC, and `65` on the first byte is the whole point of
 the line.

 Three commands rather than one, because they differ in what they
 interpolate: a bare command, one carrying a caller's mailbox name, and
 one carrying a number rendered by `show`. A conversion that handled
 literals and dropped interpolated text would pass on the first alone.

Section: Report

  iw-dump : List Integer, Integer, Integer, Text -> Text
  iw-dump (bs) (i) (n) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else iw-dump bs (i + 1) n (acc & show (list-at bs i) & " ")

  iw-line : Text -> Text
  iw-line (cmd) =
    let bs = imap-line-bytes cmd
    in show (list-length bs) & " : " & iw-dump bs 0 (list-length bs) ""

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("capability " & iw-line (imap-cmd-capability imap-new))
    print-line-uni ("select " & iw-line (imap-cmd-select imap-new "INBOX"))
    print-line-uni ("fetch " & iw-line (imap-cmd-fetch-body imap-new 7))
  end
